Ok.. here are some helpful hints to all you nethackers.. if you need to
get started and keep getting killed by stupid little mistakes, then read
this spoiler and do what it says...

There are two different methods of spoiling the game early so the rest
of the game is easy (very, very easy)..

Method 1: Find a throne room.  Kill everything in it.  Save your game.
  Make a backup of that saved game.  Restore your game and sit on the
  throne.  Either it will vanish, do nothing, genocide a monster, call
  monsters, or give you a wish.  If it vanishes, simply quit, copy your
  backup onto the saved game and restore.  If you get a wish, then save
  your game.  Likewise, if you get to genocide a monster, save it.  If
  you can have the patience (and no conscience), you could do this all
  day and rack up what would be the closest thing to an immortal mortal.
 Things to wish for:
   +3 blessed gray dragon scale mail
   +3 blessed rustproof helm of telepathy
   +3    "        "     pair of speed boots
   +3    "        "     gauntlets of power
   +3    "        "     shield of reflection (this is great!)
   +3    "    cloak of displacement (also great)
   +3    "    hawaiian shirt
   blessed amulet of life saving
   blessed ring of teleport control
   blessed ring of levitation
   blessed ring of polymorph control
   blessed bag of holding (get a lot of these)
   blessed spellbook of identify
   blessed figuring of a gray dragon (pet dragon, ehheh)

   and then your choice of the named artifacts (Sting has built in
     warning)

Method 2:  This is for the people that want to cheat, and cheat fast.
  You need to know hex for this one.  Just write down all your stats.
  Convert them to hex [for numbers larger than a 2-bit hex code, the
  order of the bits is flipped:  0A BC would actually be BC 0A, and
  0A BC DE FG would actually be FG DE BC 0A]
  edit the corresponding values in your save file to the value you want
  remember: Attributes can only go up to 25 [but, once at 25, they
  cannot be changed within the game; so, an attack that should make you
  weaker, will not].  For items, this process is even more tricky..
  the items are stored after your attributes in the save file.  Each
  item you carry has four bytes to it.  Two of the bytes indicate what
  object it is. The third byte indicates the blessing, uncursed, or
  cursed status of the object.  The fourth is the count: for weapons, it
  is a +X or a -X, for normal objects it is the count of the object.


Method 1 is easier, but method 2 is quicker and, once you have learned
it (though it took me about 3 years and a lot of versions of hack and
nethack), is much easier than method 1.

